# Copy to .env for local experiments. Do not commit .env.
# None of these are required for the site to build.
# Do not invent a key, a payment link, or a Bitcoin address.

# Server only. Used by netlify/functions/donate.ts.
# Never prefix this with PUBLIC_. A public prefix would put the secret in the site.
# STRIPE_SECRET_KEY=sk_live_...

# Set to 1 and rebuild to show the $10–$250 buttons.
# Those buttons call the function above, which also needs STRIPE_SECRET_KEY on the host.
# PUBLIC_STRIPE_CHECKOUT=1

# Stripe Payment Link (https://buy.stripe.com/...) or a donate.stripe.com link.
# When this is set, the donate page shows "Donate by card". The secret key is not required for this path.
# PUBLIC_STRIPE_PAYMENT_LINK=

# Mainnet Bitcoin address. Shown only when it looks like a real address.
# Leave this empty until an address is confirmed. Sample and placeholder values are ignored.
# PUBLIC_BITCOIN_DONATION_ADDRESS=

# Admin review queue. Server only. Never prefix these with PUBLIC_.
# The static build does not need them. /admin/login fails closed until ADMIN_PASSWORD is set.
# On Netlify: Project configuration → Environment variables. Scope them to Production
# (and to the develop site, if that site should have its own queue). Mark them secret.
# Do not invent a password or a token in this file.

# At least 12 characters. The whole value is ignored when it is a placeholder such as
# "password" or "changeme". A session cookie lasts 12 hours. Changing this signs everyone out.
# ADMIN_PASSWORD=

# Personal access token for the Netlify account that owns the site.
# It is used only on the server to read form submissions.
# Create one at https://app.netlify.com/user/applications#personal-access-tokens
# NETLIFY_AUTH_TOKEN=

# Optional. The site whose form inbox /admin/queue reads.
# Production american-forge: 13e8b163-dcb1-4638-8c3f-df186953f5a1
# Develop site american-forge-develop: 66681ebf-5a78-4af1-acb7-0d655a8e62a9
# When this is unset, the page uses Netlify's SITE_ID for whichever site is serving the page.
# The production id above is used only when neither value is present, such as a local preview.
# NETLIFY_SITE_ID=
